<Layout title="Tip Guide: Percentages, Splitting & Rounding" description="Learn how tip percentages work, how to split a bill fairly, and how to decide whether to round up."><ContentPage title="Tip guide" intro="A few simple principles make tipping easier: choose a percentage that fits the service, check the bill, and make the final amount clear."><h2>Choosing a percentage</h2><p>15%, 18%, and 20% are useful reference points for full-service restaurants. A custom amount can make sense when the setting is different or a service charge is present. Percentages are a tool, not a score for a person.</p><h2>Before tax or after tax?</h2><p>Both practices are used. The pre-tax subtotal reflects the meal or service before sales tax; using the final total is simpler and a little more generous. Enter whichever amount matches your preference.</p><h2>Splitting the bill</h2><p>Our calculator shows the amount per person and accounts for leftover cents so the displayed shares add up to the exact total. For an easy group payment, use the copy button after choosing the number of people.</p><h2>Rounding up</h2><p>The visible round-up option takes each person’s share to the next whole currency unit. It also shows how much extra the table contributes, so the choice stays transparent.</p></ContentPage></Layout>
